# Cello Suite No. 1 in G major, BWV 1007: Courante (J. S. Bach)
#
# Character: a quick Italian-style corrente in 3/4, running sixteenths
# against springing eighths and wide leaps across the strings. Bright
# and forward-moving, with a clear three to the bar.
#
# Time signature: 3/4, 42 bars with an eighth-note upbeat (bar 42 is
# short to match). Mutopia file bwv1007-2.mid, the third score of the
# set (Prelude, Allemande, Courante): checked against
# bwv1007_courante.ly. Both halves have repeat signs (A 1-18, B 19-42,
# B entered on the upbeat at the end of bar 18). The MIDI plays each
# half once, so the repeats are written out with play below.
#
# Range: written an octave up and transposed down in the score; 40 notes
# fall below B2 (the low G and D strings, e.g. bars 1-4, 18, 42) and are
# lifted an octave by the converter.
#
# Tempo: quarter = 100. With both repeats it is 252 beats, about 2:35.
# Track times (with repeats): Pablo Casals (1938) 2:10 to 2:32 by
# transfer, about 99 to 116; Pierre Fournier (Archiv, 1960) 2:45, about
# 92. Confirmed from track listings. 100 follows the slower Casals
# transfers and keeps the sixteenths clean (9 frames each).
#
# Structure (score bars; my reading of the Mutopia score):
#   A  1-8    G major, the springing opening, to D (bar 8).
#      9-18   D major: sequences, cadence in D (17-18).
#   B  19-24  From D back through G, then E minor (24).
#      25-28  A minor, D sharp diminished, E minor (28).
#      29-34  Sequences through C, A7 and D7.
#      35-42  Back in G major, the closing run and final cadence.
#
# Bars as performed (play), numbered along the performance:
#   A first  0.83-18.83   A repeat  18.83-36.83   (score bar x = x+18)
#   B first  36.83-60.83  (score x = x+18)
#   B repeat 60.83-84.83  (score x = x+42)
#
# Plan: terraced, as on two manuals: each half full the first time and
# echoed softer on the repeat, returning to the full sound for the last
# phrase (score 35) on the way home.

pickup 8
tempo 100

play 0.833333-18.833333 0.833333-18.833333 18.833333-42.833333 18.833333-42.833333

dyn 1 f              # A, first time
dyn 18.83 mp         # A repeat, an echo (from its upbeat)
broaden 35-36 0.95   # score 17-18: the D major cadence before B
dyn 36.83 f          # B, first time
dyn 60.83 mp         # B repeat, an echo
dyn 77 f             # score 35 on: home in G, full again to the end

rit 2 0.8            # the last two bars: a modest broadening
